# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: MarionOrVargaPath

translate pt strings:

    old "It was more than two weeks after the victory over the eastern tribesmen, when Sarah arrived early for a council meeting, surprised to find the room already full."
    new "Já haviam se passado mais de duas semanas desde a vitória sobre os tribais do leste quando Sarah chegou cedo para uma reunião do conselho, surpresa ao encontrar a sala já lotada."

    old "There was a busy chatter, which suddenly felt silent as everyone noticed Sarah."
    new "Havia uma conversa animada, que de repente pareceu cessar quando todos notaram Sarah."

    old "Thomas was sitting back in this throne, waiving at Sarah excitedly as she approached."
    new "Thomas estava recostado no trono, acenando animadamente para Sarah enquanto ela se aproximava."

    old "Sarah had almost reached the table, when suddenly, Marion stood up."
    new "Sarah quase havia chegado à mesa quando, de repente, Marion se levantou."

    old "Sarah saw Thomas suppress laughter. In between his laughs he managed to speak."
    new "Sarah viu Thomas reprimir uma risada. Entre as risadas, ele conseguiu falar."

    old "I believe our honorable friend, Marion, has something he wanted to say to you."
    new "Acredito que nosso honrado amigo, Marion, tem algo que gostaria de dizer a você."

    old "Sarah could feel a pit in her stomach."
    new "Sarah podia sentir um aperto no estômago."

    old "She feared she already knew what he was planning to do."
    new "Ela temia já saber o que ele planejava fazer."

    old "Confused, Sarah stared at Marion."
    new "Confusa, Sarah olhou para Marion."

    old "Marion fell to one knee, and extended a hand, holding a small box carved out of oak."
    new "Marion se ajoelhou e estendeu a mão, segurando uma pequena caixa esculpida em carvalho."

    old "Sarah Rose, having given it serious consideration, I wish to pronounce in front of all these people, my love for you."
    new "Sarah Rose, depois de ter refletido seriamente sobre o assunto, desejo declarar diante de todas estas pessoas o meu amor por ti."

    old "Please give me the honour of your hand, and I will swear to always be true."
    new "Por favor, conceda-me a honra de sua mão, e eu juro que sempre serei fiel."

    old "Stunned, Sarah felt it almost physically difficult to remain standing."
    new "Atônita, Sarah sentia que era quase fisicamente impossível permanecer de pé."

    old "The edges of her vision seemed to blur, and the ground under her feet began to shift."
    new "As bordas de sua visão pareceram se turvar, e o chão sob seus pés começou a se mover."

    old "Accept Marion's proposal."
    new "Aceitar a proposta de Marion."

    old "Yes."
    new "Sim."

    old "The words seemed to slip out before she had given it any thought."
    new "As palavras pareceram escapar antes mesmo que ela pudesse pensar nelas."

    old "She saw the faces around the table, clearly, she was not alone in her surprised."
    new "Ela viu os rostos ao redor da mesa; claramente, não estava sozinha em sua surpresa."

    old "Still on his knees, she saw Marion's face beaming."
    new "Ainda de joelhos, ela viu o rosto de Marion radiante."

    old "She watched as he rose to his feet, grabbed her by the waist and spun her around."
    new "Ela observou enquanto ele se levantava, a agarrava pela cintura e a girava."

    old "All around the room, people began to give their congratulations to the new couple."
    new "Por toda a sala, as pessoas começaram a parabenizar o novo casal."

    old "Varga was the only one who carried a pained expression on his face."
    new "Varga era o único que tinha uma expressão de dor no rosto."

    old "Sarah watched it all unfold as if this was happening to someone else."
    new "Sarah assistia a tudo aquilo como se estivesse acontecendo com outra pessoa."

    old "Reject Marion's proposal."
    new "Rejeitar a proposta de Marion."

    old "Suddenly, Sarah felt all the emotions of the shock pushed out and she found her footing again."
    new "De repente, Sarah sentiu todas as emoções do choque serem expelidas e conseguiu recuperar o equilíbrio."

    old "Rage was now keeping her tethered."
    new "A raiva era agora o que a mantinha presa."

    old "In only two broad steps she closed the distance between herself and Marion, standing over the imbecile as he was still kneeling."
    new "Em apenas dois passos largos, ela fechou a distância entre si e Marion, ficando de pé sobre o imbecil, que ainda estava ajoelhado."

    old "A more humble man would have seen the signs of what came next, but Marion was not humble."
    new "Um homem mais humilde teria percebido os sinais do que viria a seguir, mas Marion não era humilde."

    old "A shattering crack rang out across the room, followed by a deafening silence."
    new "Um estalo estrepitoso ressoou por todo o cômodo, seguido por um silêncio ensurdecedor."

    old "Marion's face was frozen off to the side, unable to process the slap, either physically or emotionally."
    new "O rosto de Marion estava congelado de lado, incapaz de processar o tapa, nem fisicamente, nem emocionalmente."

    old "Sarah could see from the corners of her eyes that everyone was staring at her."
    new "Sarah conseguia ver pelos cantos dos olhos que todos estavam olhando para ela."

    old "Marriage?"
    new "Casamento?"

    old "Are you insane?"
    new "Você está louca?"

    old "We were nothing more than friends at best, Marion."
    new "No máximo, éramos apenas amigos, Marion."

    old "I never gave you my blessing, I never agreed to any of this."
    new "Eu nunca te dei minha bênção, nunca concordei com nada disso."

    old "And if you thought I would feel forced to say yes because we were in public, you're as big of an idiot as you are craven."
    new "E se você achou que eu me sentiria obrigada a dizer sim só porque estávamos em público, você é tão idiota quanto é covarde."

    old "The only thing you've managed to do today is humiliate me, and make a joke of yourself."
    new "A única coisa que você conseguiu fazer hoje foi me humilhar e se tornar uma piada."

    old "Marion was now crawling away from her, trying to recover and get back on his feet."
    new "Marion já estava se arrastando para longe dela, tentando se recuperar e voltar a ficar de pé."

    old "By the time he had gotten onto his feet, Sarah could see his face had turned bright red."
    new "Quando ele finalmente conseguiu se levantar, Sarah podia ver que seu rosto havia ficado completamente vermelho."

    old "I brought it up with Thomas...he thought it would be..."
    new "Eu mencionei isso para Thomas... ele achou que seria..."

    old "A joke, Marion. He probably thought you were a joke, and I suppose, in that regard, he was right."
    new "É uma piada, Marion. Ele provavelmente achou que você era uma piada e, nesse sentido, acho que ele estava certo."

    old "I don't want to see you here ever again. You're off the council."
    new "Não quero mais te ver aqui nunca mais. Você está fora do conselho."

    old "Leave, and pray that nobody ever hears how much you humiliated yourself today."
    new "Saia, e reze para que ninguém jamais ouça o quanto você se humilhou hoje."

    old "Marion searched for words, but unable to find any, turned around and stormed off."
    new "Marion procurou por palavras, mas, incapaz de encontrar nenhuma, virou-se e saiu furioso."

    old "Sarah snapped back to the table full of advisors."
    new "Sarah voltou-se bruscamente para a mesa cheia de conselheiros."

    old "Her eyes ran across all the faces. Most were a mix of stunned and mortified, there was only one exception."
    new "Seus olhos percorreram todos os rostos. A maioria era uma mistura de espanto e vergonha; havia apenas uma exceção."

    old "Varga was brightly smiling, clearly having enjoyed the humiliation of Marion."
    new "Varga sorria abertamente, claramente tendo gostado da humilhação de Marion."

    old "If I find out any of you set him up to this, I swear you're going to pay for it."
    new "Se eu descobrir que algum de vocês o arranjou para isso, juro que vocês vão pagar por isso."

    old "Sarah herself now turned around and stormed off, in no mood to continue the council meeting."
    new "A própria Sarah agora se virou e saiu furiosa, sem humor para continuar a reunião do conselho."
